class: negative
summary: [1790] writes a binding's name first, on its line, so a `:=` that begins a line is a binding whose name was left out, reported there, not the line above read as a name followed by an assignment used as an expression
program: program.ldn
codes: L0100
constructs: 0390, 1790, 1810
targets: linux-x86-64, linux-arm64, macos-arm64, synthetic-32
expect: expected.txt
args: ../tests/fixtures/negative/binding-missing-its-name-is-reported-on-its-line/program.ldn
status: 1
